# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publication-workspace policy
#
# This repository is a computational research artifact. Venue-specific
# preparation -- DOCX manuscripts, final PDFs, conference figure variants,
# reviewer notes, submission metadata, templates and formatting experiments --
# belongs in an external publication workspace (see CONTRIBUTING.md), not here.
#
# These patterns prevent FUTURE local publication artifacts from being tracked;
# they do not remove files already tracked by Git.
#
# Deliberately narrow. No blanket *.docx / *.pdf / *.md rule: the research
# handbook ships as .docx, the evidence visualizations ship as .pdf, and almost
# every scientific record here is .md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
publication-local/
submission-local/
paper-drafts/
# The V1 publication workspace. CONTRIBUTING.md places publication work outside
# this computational research artifact; the evidence figures it used to hold were
# relocated beside the evidence they depict. See
# docs/provenance/V1_PUBLICATION_WORKSPACE_RETIREMENT_V1.md
docs/paper/

*_TACTiCS_*.docx
*_TACTiCS_*.pdf
*.submission.docx
*.submission.pdf
*_review_notes.md
*_review_report.md

# The curated IPS demo reproduction bundle is committed deliberately: 1.63 MiB,
# selected by scripts/provenance/select_demo_bundle.py and verified by
# reproducibility/verify_reproducibility.py. It is the only place model
# artifacts are tracked, and it exists so a reviewer can reproduce the
# demonstration from a clone plus one public ECG record.
!reproducibility/demo_bundle/**

# Generated at build time from the frozen 335-package authority.
# The generator and its proof are tracked; its output is not, so a
# stale copy can never be mistaken for the authority.
containers/j1-environment/requirements.*.txt
